#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cockpit-notifyd: the cockpit notification server (replaces mako, 2026-09-08).

Owns org.freedesktop.Notifications on the session bus, so everything (Claude,
Codex, Chrome, notify-send, cockpit-notify) lands here. Every notification is
appended to ~/.local/state/cockpit-metrics/notify-YYYY-MM.jsonl whether or not
it was shown. Cards are transient and never ask for anything: a click focuses
the source app or opens the card's link, right click dismisses, middle click
clears the screen. There is no inbox and no drawer (owner ruling, 2026-09-08:
"I shouldn't have to respond to anything through notifications").

Card anatomy: an icon (the app's own icon when it sends one, else the source's
icon, else a kind glyph), a bold title, a body, and any of the rich payloads:

  value              progress bar (the standard hint), replaced in place by group
  image-path         a picture (screenshot, render, chart), up to 400x300
  x-cockpit-kv       key/value grid          JSON [[k, v], ...]
  x-cockpit-series   bar chart / sparkline   JSON [n, n, ...]
  x-cockpit-code     monospace block         string
  x-cockpit-list     bullet list             JSON [s, ...]
  x-cockpit-icon     icon override           theme name or path
  x-cockpit-kind     info | progress | done | fail   (colours the rail)
  x-cockpit-link     URL opened on click
  x-cockpit-focus    window class focused on click
  x-cockpit-group    replace key: a new card in the same group replaces the old one

Modes: all / ai / dnd (file $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cockpit-notify/mode, or SetMode on
org.cockpit.Notify). Hidden cards are still ledgered.

Zero new packages: python-gobject (GTK3, Gio GDBus, cairo) + gtk-layer-shell.
"""
